{"term":"dumb","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:5d9d77f2631fcb4384","definition":"Unable to speak; lacking power of speech.","example":"deaf, dumb, and blind","pos":"adj","synonyms":["mute","speechless","wordless"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:22cd86c2503990755c","definition":"Not talkative; taciturn or unwilling to speak.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5d7c32ecf289c603c0","definition":"Having no input or voice in running things.","example":"Life was never a May-game for men; in all times the lot of the dumb-millions born to toil was defaced with manifold sufferings, injustices, heavy burdens, avoidable and unavoidable; not play at all, but hard work that made the sinews sore, and the heart sore.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4d40979fab3af89f71","definition":"Unaccompanied by words or speech, silent, wordless.","example":"dumb show","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated, usually","register":"dated, usually","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e24cd71ab4e3e6af5f","definition":"Not producing any sound, silent.","example":"[…] Thro’ lands where not a leaf was dumb;\n⁠But all the lavish hills would hum\nThe murmur of a happy Pan: […]","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bcabec614e3e7d1a18","definition":"Stupid.","example":"You are so dumb! You don't even know how to make toast!","pos":"adj","synonyms":["feeble-minded","idiotic","moronic","stupid","addlebrained","addlepated","airheaded","bee-brained","beef-witted","soft","beefheaded","beetle-headed","birdbrained","blockheaded","Boeotian","boneheaded","boofheaded","braindead","brainless","bubbleheaded","buffle-headed","bullet-headed","cerebrally challenged","childish","chowderheaded","chuckleheaded","crackbrained","cretinous","daft","dense","dented","dim-bulb","dim-headed","dim-witted","dim","doltish","dopey","dozy","drowsy","dull-headed","dull-minded","dull-witted","dull","dumber than a box of rocks","dumb","dunderheaded","empty-headed","fatheaded","feeble-minded","flea-brained","foolish","fuzzy-headed","fuzzy-minded","goofy","half-brained","half-witted","hammer-headed","idiotic","ignorant","imbecilic","inane","insipid","intellectually challenged","knuckleheaded","lamebrained","lowbrow","lumpish","lunkheaded","mentally challenged","mentally retarded","mindless","monosynaptic","moronic","muttonheaded","nitwitted","numbskulled","oafish","obtuse","peabrained","pratty","pudding-headed","puerile","purblind","quarter-witted","retarded","ridiculous","rockheaded","sharp as a bowling ball","sheep-headed","silly","simple","slow","slow on the uptake","slow-witted","smooth-brained","stolid","stupid","thick-skulled","thickheaded","thickwitted","thick","unapprehensive","unclever","uninformed","unintelligent","unsmart","vacant","vacuous","witless","wooden-headed","wool-headed","woolly-headed","woolly-minded","dumb as a bag of hammers","dumb as a box of rocks","dumb as a doorknob","dumb as an ox","dumb as a post","dumb as a sack of hammers","dumb as dirt","dumber than a rock","not the sharpest crayon in the box","not the sharpest knife in the drawer","not the sharpest tool in the shed","thick as a brick","thick as a plank","thick as champ","thick as mince","thick as two short planks","thick as a whale omelette","ass-brained","fuckwitted","shit-for-brains","thick as pig shit"],"antonyms":["intelligent","smart"],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, especially, informal","register":"derogatory, especially, informal","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a830926556c77add5e","definition":"Pointless, foolish, lacking intellectual content or value.","example":"This is dumb! We're driving in circles! We should have asked for directions an hour ago!","pos":"adj","synonyms":["banal","brainless","dopey","silly","stupid","ridiculous","vulgar"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3704013b1410ea6d4e","definition":"Lacking some functionality or property ordinarily characteristic of its kind.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2fbe3cbf4970f07db8","definition":"Not equipped with intelligent behavior or processing capabilities of its own.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["smart"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1f2a247c6a0e10368f","definition":"Lacking brightness or clearness as a colour; dim, dull.","example":"Her stern, which was painted of a dumb white or dun color.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, rare","register":"obsolete, rare","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f942cd36f506e08d9c","definition":"To silence.","example":"[…] what I would have spoke\nWas beastly dumbed by him.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated, transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4b8e6a2ea49e4894aa","definition":"To make stupid.","example":"I think she's dumbing us down, so we won't be smarter than her.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7b5000877bbd26b496","definition":"To represent as stupid.","example":"Bad-mouthing Neanderthals […] is symptomatic of a need to exclude and even demonize. […] I suggest that the unproven dumbing of the Neanderthals is an example of the same cultural preconception.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3c88bbec33228113b","definition":"To reduce the intellectual demands of.","example":"The ensuing storm caused the department to lower the bar—amid protests that this was dumbing the test down—so that only 80 percent of urban kids would fail.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d630946f6ede696f18","definition":"Very, extremely.","example":"\"What, you don't like your food?\" Russo asks. ¶ \"Are you kidding? It's dumb good.\"","pos":"adv","synonyms":["type","mad","hella","wicked","odee","bare"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e4c22a75c229472c05","definition":"An intensifier expressing contempt; damn, damned.","example":"Pap came to stand beside her and watched the two play. \"That pup has just plum' fell in love with our Sammy, an' Sam's real took by him,\" Pap said. \"It's a dumb shame, too. I talked to Jim, but he's not of a mind to sell.\"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dumb#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ad2337cf8b8952e264","definition":"Alternative form of D.U.M.B. (deep underground military base)","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"alt-of, alternative","register":"alt-of, alternative","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/DUMB#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8bf34b7d02775eb752","definition":"An acronym for remembering desirable characteristics for goal-setting: dream-driven, uplifting, method-driven, behavior-driven.","example":"Whatever your goals, starting with a DUMB goal gives a great outline and starting off point to start building your plan of action.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"mnemonic, not-comparable","register":"mnemonic, not-comparable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/DUMB#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/dʌm/"},"wordFamily":[]}